# Responsibility: Define a robot- and backend-independent reactive pose-tracking task.
#
# The server moves its configured controlled frame toward target_pose while
# continuously reacting to the current robot state. The action does not name a
# robot, controller, planner, command transport, or Servo implementation.

# Desired pose of the server-configured controlled frame. header.frame_id is
# the task reference frame in which this pose and feedback errors are evaluated.
# It must be a canonical relative frame name without a leading slash.
# header.stamp must be normalized and non-zero. Every pose component must be
# finite and the quaternion must have unit norm. If the backend commands in
# another frame, it must resolve the target with TF at that exact ROS timestamp;
# falling back to latest TF is forbidden. The resolved target remains fixed for
# the lifetime of the goal and is not retargeted by later TF updates.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped target_pose

# Zero selects the server-configured timeout. A positive value must be longer
# than the server's reserved safe-stop budget; shorter goals are rejected before
# resource acquisition. An accepted value creates one steady-clock deadline
# covering validation, resource acquisition, tracking, cooperative pauses, and
# the final bounded stop. ROS time pauses or resets do not extend it, and time
# spent paused still consumes the deadline.
builtin_interfaces/Duration timeout
---
# Motion-only terminal result. Success means the configured pose tolerance was
# reached, stop_confirmed was established from fresh velocity samples plus a
# confirmed backend pause, and new post-stop pose samples remained in tolerance.
MotionTaskResult result
---
# Standard task lifecycle, progress, pause state, and steady elapsed time.
ManipulationTaskState state

# True only when both following error values were computed from one current,
# frame-consistent robot-state sample. Clients must ignore both values when
# false. A server sets this false while no fresh sample or required TF exists.
bool tracking_error_valid

# Non-negative finite Euclidean translation error in metres, evaluated in the
# task frame. Meaningful only when tracking_error_valid is true.
float64 linear_error_m

# Non-negative finite shortest rotation error in radians, in [0, pi] and
# evaluated in the task frame. Meaningful only when tracking_error_valid is true.
float64 angular_error_rad

# Pause is cooperative: on a SetTaskPaused request the server stops issuing
# motion commands, reports pause_pending until a bounded stop is confirmed, and
# then reports paused. Resume tracks the same fixed target from the live robot
# state. Cancel takes priority over pause/resume and similarly reaches a bounded
# confirmed stop before returning CANCELED; failure to stop is reported as an
# execution or recovery failure. Stale state or TF must trigger the same stop
# path instead of continuing open-loop.
